## How online payment works

When you pay a fee from your dashboard, you're taken to a payment page in a new tab to enter your
card details. Keep that tab open until the payment finishes — closing it partway through can leave
the payment in an unclear state.

## After you pay

Once the payment completes, you're redirected back to a confirmation page showing the transaction
ID, a masked version of the card used, and the amount charged. This confirmation is your proof of
payment even before it shows up in your school's records.

If your fee doesn't show as paid within a short while after a successful payment, contact your
school's office with the **transaction ID** from the confirmation page — that's what staff use to
look up and manually reconcile a payment that hasn't synced automatically (see
[Accounting Workflow](/docs/shared-staff-accounting-overview) for the staff-facing side of this).

## Payment not showing as an option

If you don't see a fee you were expecting to pay online, the school may not have enabled online
payment for that particular fee yet — this is a per-fee setting, not something you can turn on
yourself. Contact your school's office rather than assuming it's an app problem.
